[0, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  /  attached volume conversion\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;245m  Ubuntu 24.04  ·  1 GiB RAM  ·  DigitalOcean  ·  existing files preserved\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m  01  A normal attached ext4 volume\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  $ lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS\r\n  NAME     SIZE FSTYPE  MOUNTPOINTS\r\n  sda        1G ext4    /mnt/data\r\n  vda       25G         \r\n  |-vda1    24G ext4    /\r\n  |-vda14    4M         \r\n  |-vda15  106M vfat    /boot/efi\r\n  `-vda16  913M ext4    /boot\r\n  vdb      488K iso9660 \r\n  \r\n  $ df -h /mnt/data\r\n  Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\r\n  /dev/sda        974M  181M  727M  20% /mnt/data\u001b[31;1H\u001b[38;5;245m  Actual output · waits shortened · development build · full recording linked below\u001b[0m"]
